From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:21:01 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] ASoC: samsung: add the Galaxy A50 ABOX sound card

A machine driver for the ABOX card of the Galaxy A50 (SM-A505F), with
the DAI link layout of the stock vogue-rt5665 driver so the vendor audio
HAL finds the same card: name "Exynos9610-Audio", RDMA0-7 and WDMA0-4 as
DPCM front ends (ALSA devices 0-12; RDMA5 is the compress device) and
UAIF0/1/2/4, DSIF, SPDY and SIFS0-2 as back ends. The ABOX components get
the "ABOX" name prefix and the ABOX effect block is an auxiliary device,
as on stock, so the controls keep the names the HAL mixer paths use.

Each link's DAIs come from a child of the sound node named after the
link; without a "codec" child the link uses the dummy codec. The codec
and amplifier links (RT5665, TFA9872) are added later.

6.18 adaptations of the stock driver:
- links built from DT with snd_soc_of_get_dlc() and the dummy dlc;
- the Samsung POST_PRE/PRE_POST trigger orders become mainline POST
  (playback) and PRE (capture), which give the same order;
- 6.18 calls be_hw_params_fixup() without the stream, so a wrapper
  finds the stream whose front end is updating the back end and passes
  it to abox_hw_params_fixup_helper();
- back-end formats and clock roles from the generic "format",
  "bitclock-master" and "frame-master" properties.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Idbe775549bd0dbc90dfc423555027bce3255f6c9
